# What NOT to send to the Docker daemon when building.
#
# Everything not listed here is copied into the build context and then into the
# image by `COPY . .`. Three reasons to be strict: build speed, image size, and
# above all secrecy -- .env and the SSH key must never end up in a layer, and a
# layer cannot be un-published once the image is pushed anywhere.

# Secrets and keys. Never, under any circumstances.
.env
.env.*
*.pem

# The live database. It belongs on the host, bind-mounted in, so that rebuilding
# the image cannot destroy the league's data.
db.sqlite3
db.sqlite3-journal
db/

# Local virtualenv: Windows binaries, useless and large in a Linux image.
.venv/

# Build artefacts and caches -- collectstatic runs inside the build.
staticfiles/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# History and tooling the running site has no use for.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.vscode/
.idea/

# Source data and analysis. The importers that read these run locally; the
# tidy CSVs in data/processed are small and stay, so an import can be re-run
# on the server if it ever needs to be.
data/raw/
notebooks/
src/

# The rules doc is READ AT REQUEST TIME by the rules view, so docs/ must stay
# in the image. Do not add it here.
